1
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:13,340
Try lightening up on peace
and stepping away from it

2
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:26,880
aiming for a certain day
floating on the Nakagawa

3
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:33,980
when I kick a pebble, even my shoes fly off

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,240
And to the carpenters'
boss who had been saving up

5
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that I'm still just a kid

6
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:53,560
even if I pass on some energy somewhere

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,640
Katsushika-ku Kameari,
one yawn, nothing changes

8
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:02,540
the streetscape is strangely kind

9
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:10,500
from the pointed-hat water tank

10
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:16,800
the sunset sinks toward
the great stone observatory

11
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:25,260
Why does tomorrow end too, huh

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,280
Hey, Katsushika or Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost

13
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:34,020
I realized, because I'm such a fool

14
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:41,660
Kameari's night is gentle,

15
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:51,580
What the heck is this!

16
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,780
a chill runs down your spine, that one...

17
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:57,240
Isn't that one of those
wife-made lunch boxes?

18
00:01:57,240 --> 00:01:57,880
No need to be shy.

19
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:58,940
Well, yeah.

20
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:02,900
I said I didn't want it,

21
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,200
but you went and made it anyway, didn't you?

22
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:05,920
Here you go, dear.

23
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:10,640
The progress of the Japanese diet

24
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:12,060
as if mocking it

25
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:13,720
that old-fashioned wife-made lunch box

26
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:16,660
still survives, like something from the end of the century.
I never expected it.

27
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:18,320
Ryo-san, your late-night snack

28
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,340
As for me, the night-shift snack is...

29
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:28,580
I've decided on ramen, Terae-kun. Look, these are the
three items I prepared for tonight's midnight snack.

30
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:39,920
Of course cup noodles are the smart midnight snack.
Ever since cup noodles debuted as a revolutionary emergency food that packs high energy into a small amount, it's been nearly 30

31
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:48,800
years. With a wide range of menus, from Japanese and Western to Chinese,
they made it possible to enjoy freshly boiled noodles with professional flavor using minimal effort.

32
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:51,060
The progress of cup noodles in recent years

33
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:55,220
is truly a miracle bestowed by heaven.

34
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,380
It's worthy of a Nobel Prize.

35
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:03,800
With such Nobel-worthy food around,

36
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:07,400
I can't understand anyone who would eat a cold,
wife-made bento.

37
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:10,460
So your wife came to Ryo-san's place and

38
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:12,520
she went and made one more, but

39
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:14,200
you won't eat it, right?

40
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,840
It's fine, I'll eat both of them.

41
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:23,540
Ramen, yakisoba, kitsune udon...
alright, which one should I start with?

42
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:25,840
Before that,
I'll go put some water on to boil.

43
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:40,680
Add the freeze-dried
ingredients and the soup base,

44
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,720
and with that, everything's ready.

45
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:49,760
"Don't eat it? Good luck!"
Your wife-made bento can wait.

46
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:52,780
Once the water boils,
I'll make some tea and eat.

47
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:57,980
I'll have you know that water's boiling for my cup ramen,
so don't get any ideas.

48
00:03:57,980 --> 00:04:00,840
There should be enough
left over for tea, right?

49
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:06,060
Sorry, I only boiled exactly
enough water for one bowl of ramen.

50
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:10,100
Factoring in what evaporates, it's 455cc.

51
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:13,060
So there's none left over, nope.

52
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,460
Really? Well, fine then.

53
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:22,960
For a late-night snack, nothing beats
hot ramen over a cold bento, right?

54
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:27,600
It's warm because it's
full of my wife's love.

55
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:36,960
Good folks of the neighborhood, here's a man eating
an embarrassing wife-made bento in this day and age!

56
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:40,940
Good folks of the neighborhood,
it's a wife-made bento!

57
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:43,200
Don't stop, Ryo-san!
It's too much of a nuisance!

58
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:46,440
What are you doing? Are you trying
to silence my freedom of speech?

59
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:49,340
A wife-made bento, you say?

60
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:52,340
A wife-made bento

61
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,580
Uh-oh, trouble's coming.

62
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:56,020
What should we do, Ryo-san?

63
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:57,260
Just pretend you don't see him.

64
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,178
So,

65
00:05:00,228 --> 00:05:03,700
Where's the wife-made bento?

66
00:05:05,020 --> 00:05:06,180
Right here?

67
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:10,600
Is it yours?

68
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:15,820
Very good.

69
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:16,920
Passed.

70
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:18,480
Thanks.

71
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:22,720
Is this also a wife-made bento, I wonder?

72
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:25,980
How is this a wife-made bento?

73
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:28,980
Judging by that face, you're still single.

74
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:30,700
What a pitiful man.

75
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:32,860
Don't judge by looks alone.

76
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:36,460
I want to find a wife quickly and
have her make me a wife-made bento.

77
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:38,480
Mind your own business!

78
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,028
First of all, if you get a wife,

79
00:05:40,078 --> 00:05:42,920
it doesn't mean a bento comes with her,
you know!

80
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:48,640
In other words, you're a family treasure.

81
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,280
Congratulations!

82
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:55,040
What's this
"hurry up and get a wife" nonsense?

83
00:05:58,380 --> 00:05:59,460
Got it!

84
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:06,660
While I was dealing with that drunk,
the hot water evaporated.

85
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:08,820
Maybe you didn't put enough water in.

86
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:09,360
So annoying.

87
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,440
Are you all right?

88
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:17,580
Hey, don't let him sleep there, Terai!

89
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:23,520
Pour boiling water up to the inner line,
then wait four minutes.

90
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:25,860
Just four minutes, and no wife required!

91
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:26,900
Help!

92
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:30,480
Your wife?

93
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:31,980
N-no, it's not!

94
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,080
Hurry, hurry, come quick!

95
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:36,480
Wait, explain what happened!

96
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,760
Someone came in!

97
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:41,960
Someone suddenly came into my room!

98
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:44,940
What? An intruder in a young woman's room?

99
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:46,940
Ryo-san, it's your strong point!

100
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:49,240
So, a burglar? Or a pervert?

101
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:50,180
It's a cockroach!

102
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,740
You idiot!

103
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:55,340
Don't come here over something like that,
you dumb ass.

104
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,960
But there's no one else I can ask.

105
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:02,320
Protecting citizens' lives is the police's job,
isn't it?

106
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:07,640
Things like that fall under the health center or ward office,
not the police.

107
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:11,760
The health center and ward office
aren't open at this hour, either.

108
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:16,080
If Ryo-san can keep an eye on this guy,
I'll go get help.

109
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:34,200
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

110
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:39,320
I'll be right back,
so be a good boy and wait for me.

111
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,580
So, do you live nearby?

112
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:43,900
Yes, that apartment building over there.

113
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:46,060
Where is it?

114
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:48,828
A black one about 5 centimeters long,

115
00:07:48,878 --> 00:07:51,440
scurried behind the stereo.

116
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:52,900
Here?

117
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:56,260
It's not here. There's no sign of it at all.

118
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,220
That can't be right.

119
00:07:58,220 --> 00:08:01,700
It must be clinging to something somewhere.
Look properly.

120
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,260
It's fine, it won't come out again.

121
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:06,100
How can you be so sure?

122
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:08,420
What if it comes out again?

123
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:10,920
Even if a cockroach shows up,
it's not going to kill you.

124
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,840
Besides, it's almost three minutes.

125
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:16,280
Make sure you exterminate
it properly before you leave.

126
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:19,300
I hate people who do things halfway.

127
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,140
Hate away, then.

128
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:24,180
I'm neither your apprentice nor your lover,
you know.

129
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:27,180
Please, I'll make you some coffee.

130
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:29,640
Hey, don't go home.

131
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:35,160
Just sit here, it'll be ready in a moment.

132
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:42,240
Maybe the cockroach
thing can wait until later?

133
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:44,020
Could it be that woman is...

134
00:08:46,220 --> 00:08:48,500
trying to seduce me?

135
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:53,360
She's been interested in me
while I'm on duty for a while now,

136
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:57,000
and if she's been waiting for a chance
to catch me on the night shift...

137
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:04,540
Here you go, officer, sugar?

138
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:07,320
No, I'm fine.

139
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:11,140
No doubt about it,
I'm being seduced right now.

140
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:15,040
That's right, want to hear some tips?

141
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:18,060
I love music too.

142
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:20,360
Especially Saburo Kitajima
and people like that.

143
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:22,740
That's not really the case.

144
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:25,620
It's because of things like this, you know.

145
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:31,360
Here you go, dear, your bento.

146
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:33,780
Come home early, okay?

147
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:40,940
It's out!

148
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:41,920
Whoa!

149
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:46,100
I quit!

150
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:47,960
It's here!

151
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,320
Wah!

152
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:00,940
Thank you very much, officer.

153
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,380
Good luck with your work.

154
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:07,900
Good luck with your work, you idiot.

155
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:18,540
It's gone soggy and cold,
but it's still good, right?

156
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,100
Hey, Terai.

157
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,040
Welcome back, Ryo-san.

158
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:27,720
Ryo-san.

159
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,800
Don't "welcome back" me.

160
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:31,320
What do you think you're doing
drinking sake without permission?

161
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,900
I'm not drinking.

162
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:35,320
No, I'm in really good spirits.

163
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:37,520
Terai and I really hit it off.

164
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,080
Mrs. Sasaki,
the wife of Mr. Sasaki, she's...

165
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:42,280
She's a great cook, beautiful, and so kind.

166
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:46,220
Who's stupid enough to take someone else's
lovey-dovey stories seriously and be happy about it?

167
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:48,640
On your marks...
a single man's long-held wish comes true!

168
00:10:50,660 --> 00:10:51,840
Suit yourself.

169
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:55,280
Then pour it up to the inner line.

170
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,140
Once three minutes have passed,

171
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:09,800
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

172
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:14,740
I didn't say that. Ryo-san,
Sasaki-san really has it rough, you know.

173
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:19,280
I'm stepping out for a bit, so once three minutes are up,
dump the yakisoba water for me.

174
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:22,980
Got it, I'll dump it. Just dump it.

175
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:26,800
Don't you dare forget! Three minutes,
I'm telling you, three minutes!

176
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:32,100
So these are the ones causing the fight?

177
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:35,580
It's so noisy I can't sleep.
Do something about it, officer!

178
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:36,940
Well, what can you do.

179
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:38,660
Hey, get away from him!

180
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:40,340
Get off!

181
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:44,160
Eeh! That hurts!

182
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:46,540
Get a grip, officer!

183
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:48,600
This bastard, I'm not forgiving him!

184
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:02,780
Now, where the hell did he go?

185
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,420
Suspicious guy!

186
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:24,480
Hey, what do you think you're doing there!

187
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:26,820
Hey, don't run!

188
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,700
What's your name and address?

189
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:33,900
My name's Matsufuji.
My address is right here.

190
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:34,200
See?

191
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:36,800
This is my home.

192
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:39,440
If it's your home,
why were you sneaking around peeking inside?

193
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:42,051
I came home late after drinking,

194
00:12:42,101 --> 00:12:44,779
and my wife locked the door chain on me,

195
00:12:44,829 --> 00:12:46,800
and she's probably asleep by now.

196
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:49,620
What should I do?

197
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:54,140
Wake up your wife. If you don't want to do that,
you can sleep out here on the street.

198
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:55,720
That's a bit much...

199
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:58,020
Not my problem. Do whatever you want.

200
00:12:58,020 --> 00:13:00,840
W-wait, Officer!

201
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:02,980
Please come apologize to my wife with me!

202
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:06,880
Why the hell would I have
to apologize to your wife?!

203
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:08,840
Please!

204
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:13,360
My wife might forgive me
if an officer is with me!

205
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,300
Please! Please! Please!

206
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:18,920
Is your wife really that strict?

207
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:25,460
What's so wrong about having a drink after
a day's work and coming home a little late?

208
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:26,740
R-right, isn't it!

209
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:30,560
Hey, why are you scared of your missus?

210
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:34,120
If you're a man,
show her some manly backbone!

211
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:35,480
Y-yeah! Alright!

212
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:42,860
Who do you think I am!

213
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:46,200
W-well, I, I was, I was working overtime!

214
00:13:46,340 --> 00:13:51,320
I-I just saw that drunk husband home,
so, well then...

215
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:57,760
I'm in too deep now.
Please keep me company, officer.

216
00:13:57,840 --> 00:14:00,460
No way! I have nothing to do with this!

217
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:06,060
You came home drunk again, didn't you!

218
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:10,700
Cut it out!
Is it so bad to have a few drinks?

219
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:12,760
A man has to keep up his drinking buddies...

220
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:16,820
Don't you dare butt into
other people's marriages!

221
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:20,600
I won't forgive even this woman!

222
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:27,440
Ugh

223
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,240
Please don't resist.

224
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:32,580
My wife was a former women's
pro wrestling world champion.

225
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:33,620
W-what?

226
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:34,160
See?

227
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:42,220
You bastard, why didn't you say that sooner?

228
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:44,740
What do you think you're
doing to my husband?

229
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:46,320
No your husband...

230
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:49,180
No, I mean, your husband should
avoid drinking alcohol and such,

231
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:53,100
so he gets home early.
That's why I'm giving this lecture.

232
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,000
Ow ow!

233
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:56,500
You're lecturing my husband?

234
00:14:56,660 --> 00:14:59,620
No, well,
alcohol is bad for your health, after all.

235
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:11,700
Mind your own business!

236
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:15,520
Aaaaah!

237
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:16,260
Aaaaah!

238
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:16,920
Ni

239
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,300
Aaaaaaah

240
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:32,480
Aaaaaaah

241
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:35,860
Aaaaaaah

242
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:35,920
Aaaaaaah

243
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:37,140
What the hell are you doing?!

244
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,120
And now, the match is about to begin!

245
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:39,960
Hey!

246
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:49,240
Whoa! A flowing series of moves!

247
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:52,160
What do you think,
commentator Miru Tabigara?!

248
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:55,740
There's not a hint of decline since her active days,
is there?

249
00:15:57,520 --> 00:16:00,640
How could you marry a woman like this?!

250
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:02,740
I was a huge fan!

251
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:04,360
No matter how big a fan you were...

252
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:06,790
Well, you see,

253
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:10,340
If you marry me, I'll do anything you say!

254
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:13,240
I said I'd even die for you!

255
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:16,760
Is it coming?!
The finishing Death Valley Bomb!

256
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,780
This'll be over with one blow!

257
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:20,380
Okay!

258
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:30,420
Champion retains the title!

259
00:16:30,420 --> 00:16:32,080
Whoa!

260
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:34,060
You!

261
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:35,980
You bastard!

262
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:38,620
I love you!

263
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:41,820
Why does this have to happen to me!

264
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:46,120
My, my...

265
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:49,780
My yakisoba... w-welcome back...

266
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:53,120
No! What are you doing!

267
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,080
Ryo-san, sorry.

268
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:58,580
It spilled because you didn't
hold the lid down properly!

269
00:17:00,980 --> 00:17:02,320
Wait! You clumsy idiot!

270
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:05,160
And why are you dumping the hot water now,
of all times?

271
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:07,760
Three minutes passed long ago, you know!

272
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:10,280
I got caught up chatting with Sasagyo...

273
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:15,667
"Caught up," my foot! Do you have any idea what I went through,
leaving my yakisoba right after pouring in the hot water,

274
00:17:15,717 --> 00:17:16,960
do you?

275
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:20,312
It felt like my body was being cut open,

276
00:17:20,362 --> 00:17:22,720
like my very life force
was being torn apart,

277
00:17:22,770 --> 00:17:26,020
a bitter, heartbreaking feeling.

278
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:29,000
Ryo-san, I'm sorry.

279
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:29,620
Forget it.

280
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:33,300
I was a fool to trust someone like Terai.

281
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:36,140
I let you end up in this state.

282
00:17:37,180 --> 00:17:40,240
Forgive me, please, forgive me.

283
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:44,560
It tastes like tears.

284
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:48,420
I'm seriously starving.

285
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:50,860
This time, third time's the charm.

286
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:52,920
It won't light!

287
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:55,680
What is this hose?

288
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:03,140
Ugh, it reeks of gas!

289
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:04,040
Sasaki-san!

290
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:07,860
Don't stop me!

291
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,040
Why would you do something like this?

292
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:13,000
Who's the idiot who'd kill himself
on a whim while drunk at night!

293
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:16,490
Buried in work, neglecting his home,

294
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:19,480
his beloved wife ran off,
and it's been three months already.

295
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:22,940
Let her go, let her go! Wives?
Just let them all run off!

296
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:24,000
Ryo-san!

297
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:27,980
Ever since, he's lost interest in
work and let his life fall apart,

298
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:30,420
and living alone as a
man has reached its limit.

299
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:33,140
Going back to an empty home is too painful,

300
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:34,420
so he ends up drinking heavily...

301
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:39,040
I feel like there's nothing good left,
even if I keep on living like this.

302
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:40,140
So,

303
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:43,380
Sure, there are hard
times when you're alive,

304
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:46,520
but there must be far
more enjoyable things too.

305
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:47,500
Sasaki-san.

306
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:51,180
As long as I have this,
I don't need some troublesome wife.

307
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:54,760
This time, no matter what happens,
I won't leave your side.

308
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:55,660
*Pnyuu*

309
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:57,780
This is my wife.

310
00:18:57,780 --> 00:18:59,240
She's beautiful.

311
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:02,560
Yeah, I can see why you'd brag.

312
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:05,840
Said to be a beauty on par with Reiko Ohara,
Yuko Asano,

313
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:08,460
and Norika Fujiwara combined,

314
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:10,060
she was a favorite around the neighborhood.

315
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:13,100
She loved cleaning and
laundry above all else,

316
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:15,960
and her cooking was on par with a chef's.

317
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:18,280
Her personality was cheerful and honest.

318
00:19:19,540 --> 00:19:20,980
Everyone liked her,

319
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:24,900
she was a wife too good for me.

320
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:27,820
Let's keep hope, Sasaki-san.

321
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:30,220
Maybe your wife is somewhere right now,

322
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:32,160
regretting leaving home,

323
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:35,300
and one day she might just come back.

324
00:19:35,660 --> 00:19:36,000
Yeah, I suppose so.

325
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:41,860
Nah, your missus is probably
living a happy life worthy of a beauty,

326
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:43,820
living a happy life worthy of a beauty,

327
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:46,320
surely toasting with champagne.

328
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:47,920
Ryo-san

329
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:01,940
Sasaki's wife isn't that kind of person.

330
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:04,060
Someone as beautiful as her

331
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:07,480
marrying you,
who isn't even a millionaire, was already

332
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:08,780
like an accident.

333
00:20:08,780 --> 00:20:12,540
A sensible adult would have
realized that before getting married.

334
00:20:12,540 --> 00:20:15,340
Consider it a nice dream and give up on it.

335
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,800
That's just Ryo-san's prejudice.

336
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:20,240
Ryo-san, who has never been married once,

337
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:22,280
how could you possibly understand
what a married couple is like?

338
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:23,940
Well, I don't want to understand.

339
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:28,140
The night shift is calling me.

340
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:33,220
So my wife really isn't
coming back after all.

341
00:20:33,660 --> 00:20:34,300
I'm going to die.

342
00:20:35,820 --> 00:20:38,340
Please don't mind what Ryo-san said.

343
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:40,940
Don't stop me, don't stop me, don't stop me!

344
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:44,300
Sorry for being so rude, Sasaki-san, but

345
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:46,800
Ryo-san,
stop saying things that just set him off!

346
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:48,300
Right, this time I'm really going to eat!

347
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:49,900
Damn it!

348
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:51,900
Farewell.

349
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:53,940
I said stop it!

350
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:56,720
If I'm going to die, then I'm going to die!

351
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:58,120
Sasaki-san!

352
00:20:58,140 --> 00:20:59,160
I'm dying! I'm dying!

353
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:00,200
Ryo-san, stop him too!

354
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:02,240
Don't worry, Terai.

355
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:04,140
Someone who's really set on dying

356
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:05,600
wouldn't come to a place like this.

357
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:07,880
Right, time's up.

358
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:10,420
I'm dying! I'm dying! I'm dying!

359
00:21:10,420 --> 00:21:10,620
Hey!

360
00:21:12,940 --> 00:21:13,660
Bon appétit!

361
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:15,740
I mean it!

362
00:21:24,620 --> 00:21:26,060
Aaaaaah!

363
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:27,120
Aaaaaah!

364
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:35,980
Ryo-san, my kitsune udon...

365
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:43,160
Damn you, I won't forgive you!
I'll die! I'll die! I'll die!

366
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:43,640
Wait!

367
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:45,900
Sasaki!

368
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:48,600
Don't stop me!

369
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:51,960
Who's stopping you? I'll help you!

370
00:21:53,060 --> 00:21:54,060
Help!

371
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,620
Hey, wait!

372
00:21:58,760 --> 00:21:59,780
Murderer!

373
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:01,940
Wait!

374
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:03,460
No!

375
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:05,140
Stop it!

376
00:22:06,140 --> 00:22:07,840
I said wait, damn it!

377
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:08,920
I said no, damn it!

378
00:22:11,860 --> 00:22:13,940
You idiot! You want to die?!

379
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:23,120
Help, help, help, I can't swim, help me!

380
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:25,600
You wanted to die,
so this is perfect, isn't it?

381
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,540
I don't want to die yet!

382
00:22:27,540 --> 00:22:28,580
Sasaki-san!

383
00:22:30,340 --> 00:22:32,680
Hang on, we're saving you right now!

384
00:22:35,860 --> 00:22:37,080
Help me, help me!

385
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:37,800
Ryo-san!

386
00:22:40,220 --> 00:22:40,980
Ryo-san!

387
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:42,620
Well, there's no choice.

388
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:45,660
Here you go, grab on quick!

389
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:47,000
Ryo-san!

390
00:22:48,860 --> 00:22:50,040
One at a time!

391
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:54,260
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa! Wait! Cola!

392
00:22:54,820 --> 00:22:55,820
Aaaaaaaah!

393
00:23:01,660 --> 00:23:02,380
Good morning.

394
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:04,920
Chief, good morning.

395
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:05,140
Good morning.

396
00:23:05,613 --> 00:23:09,400
Weren't Ryotsu and Terai on duty until noon?

397
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:11,465
Well, Terai called me and said,

398
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:15,120
he's coming down with a cold and
asked if we could switch shifts.

399
00:23:15,980 --> 00:23:18,400
I see. And what about Ryotsu?

400
00:23:18,740 --> 00:23:20,700
Senpai is

401
00:23:25,020 --> 00:23:27,700
Honestly, what a pathetic guy.

402
00:23:27,820 --> 00:23:30,700
No matter how much I call out to him,
he won't wake up.

403
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:32,460
He must be really exhausted.

404
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:36,675
That can't be. The duty log is blank, too.

405
00:23:36,725 --> 00:23:40,140
He must have been out partying all night.

406
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:42,720
Ramen...

407
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:45,360
Because he's not married
and just drifting along,

408
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:48,880
he'll never develop a sense of
responsibility as a member of society.

409
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:50,020
Hey, Ryotsu!

410
00:23:50,860 --> 00:23:53,080
Pour out the yakisoba water, will you?

411
00:23:53,980 --> 00:23:55,040
Bakabon!

412
00:23:55,860 --> 00:23:57,960
How long are you going to
keep having your sweet dreams?

413
00:23:57,960 --> 00:23:59,540
Wake up, Ryotsu!

414
00:24:13,560 --> 00:24:27,340
Even in the dead of night, when your
call comes, I wake up feeling good.

415
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:41,800
Even dull talk sets my whole body aflame,
but I still want to see my friends.

416
00:24:43,140 --> 00:24:52,600
I surely want to be loved, just enough
to make everyone a little jealous.

417
00:24:52,600 --> 00:24:58,320
Feeling as if we're
melting into one another.

418
00:24:58,320 --> 00:25:07,960
I surely want to confess, but somehow,
when it comes to love, I'm timid.

419
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:15,820
Don't hide everything behind your bravado.

420
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:24,160
Chief! Why do I have to
play golf of all things!

421
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:27,120
Listen, Ryotsu!
The Chief is a huge golf fan!

422
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:29,240
Whatever happens, don't go playing well!

423
00:25:29,340 --> 00:25:30,440
How can you say that!

424
00:25:30,660 --> 00:25:32,660
H-hey! What's with these guys!

425
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:35,560
Next time: showdown! The golf course raid!

426
00:25:35,740 --> 00:25:37,180
Counting on you, Ryotsu!

427
00:25:42,260 --> 00:25:43,660
Thank you for watching.

